# ── PII: never commit entrant lists or the live built page ────────
# The raffle entrant CSV holds real names and email addresses. build.py
# inlines that CSV (and the fonts/logos) into index.html, so the live
# built page contains the same PII. Both stay local only.
#
# Any CSV here is treated as a real entrant list by default. The one
# exception is valkey-raffle.sample.csv, which contains only fake data.
*.csv
!*.sample.csv

# Live, self-contained raffle page (inlines the real entrant CSV → PII).
# The committed, PII-safe equivalent is index.template.html, built from the
# sample CSV with `python3 build.py --template`.
index.html

# Local Python bytecode from running or inspecting the builder.
__pycache__/
